# Audit-warning acknowledgement ledger — T-3167
#
# arc-008's bar is that every remaining audit warning is "fixed OR explicitly
# acknowledged with a cited reason". This file is the second half. Entries here are
# COUNTED AND REPORTED by scripts/check-audit-warning-acknowledgement.sh and do not
# fire; they are never hidden, because a ledger that hides findings is the global
# kill switch it replaces.
#
# Format:   <drift-stable pattern>  # <cited reason>
#
# The pattern is a case-sensitive SUBSTRING of the audit's `check` text. Use the
# check's NAME, never its numbers. Audit check strings embed volatile counts
# ("93 GO-scope-not-propagated ... of 176", "297/535 cards"), and a pattern
# carrying a count silently stops matching the moment the count moves — that exact
# drift is what made T-3117's premise expire unnoticed. The checker reports an
# entry that matches nothing as a `stale-entry`, so rot is visible rather than silent.
#
# An entry is only appropriate when the finding is REAL and we are structurally
# barred from fixing it here. Anything fixable gets fixed, not listed. Each entry
# must state what would let it be deleted — an acknowledgement with no exit
# condition is a permanent exemption wearing a reason as a disguise.
#
# A FAIL can never be acknowledged. The arc's bar is zero failures.

